add(22,'P2','N','Research formulas are image-only and several are physically cropped','AntiRL Coaching Evidence Research.md','![][image6]','80 embedded formula PNGs cannot be searched/diffed/accessibly read; important summation/share/boost formulas are cut off at their right boundary in original image files. Reviewers cannot recover exact constraints from those images alone.', 'Extract image6/11/15/31/36 and composite on white; originals end mid-expression.', 'Threshold text exists elsewhere but formula images themselves omit trailing expressions and labels.', 'Replace formula images with versioned plaintext/LaTeX and test vectors; reduce root report to decision history linked to source-backed ADRs.',effort='S',evidence='review/research-formulas/white-0.png')
add(23,'P2','O','Research mode cards prescribe absolute tactics and unvalidated numeric outcomes','AntiRL Coaching Evidence Research.md','short drill: Low-Risk Shadow Defense Scrimmage','The report calls its cards evidence-grounded but prescribes absolute no-flip ranked play, fixed midfield limits, zero kickoff goals and universal boost/recovery thresholds. It also says 36 boost enables any save. These are hypotheses, not calibrated detector or coaching facts; the repository audit deliberately rejected them.', 'Read section03 plus extracted images38..54, and RESEARCH_AUDIT mode-card rejection.', 'Unverified tactical heuristics are written as guarantees and target metrics; citations do not validate numeric cutoffs.', 'Keep drill constraints as optional authored experiments with exceptions; support direct replay observations and expert-reviewed annotations; do not import universal targets.',effort='M',evidence='review/research-formulas/white-1.png; review/research-formulas/white-2.png; docs/archive/reviews/RESEARCH_AUDIT.md')
add(24,'P2','O','Research over-abstention conflates no calibrated forecast with no useful comparison','AntiRL Coaching Evidence Research.md','* *Cross-Sectional Confounding*','The report overstates evidence restrictions (e.g. cross-sectional expert comparison provides zero information and strict one observation for every tactical question). Avoiding unsupported grades/forecasts is correct, but prohibits descriptive personal baselines and multi-moment explanations that can help the player.', 'Read sections00/02/08 and self-critique beside prior research audit rejection of categorical impossibility.', 'Research often substitutes a universal ban for bounded claim language; current product inherits long caveats instead of useful low-risk coaching.', 'Separate measured personal changes, estimated hypotheses and calibrated comparisons; permit 2–3 evidence moments supporting one priority, with optional method details.',effort='M')
add(25,'P2','O','Native decoded kickoff/pad/stat data is underused for practical coaching','crates/replay-core/src/lib.rs','StatsCollector::with_builtin_module_names(["touch"])','Only touch statistics are requested from the decoder graph; native pad pickups, shot geometry and controller capture exist, but report focuses on average boost/speed/half share. Kickoff outcomes, pad-pathing, recovery windows and you-versus-opponent deltas are absent from the main report.', 'Compare captured pad_events/shots/controller fields to hero metrics and event detector inventory.', 'High-value available facts do not create next actions; unvalidated research panels compete for attention.', 'Prioritize kickoff timelines, pad-route opportunities, recovery speed and direct comparative event evidence; stage 50/50/touch-quality hypotheses behind annotated validation.',effort='L')
existing=set()
p=Path('review/findings.jsonl')
if p.exists():
 for l in p.read_text(encoding='utf-8').splitlines():
  try:existing.add(json.loads(l)['id'])
  except:pass
for x in items:
 if x['id'] not in existing:finding(**x)
Path('review/parser-findings.json').write_text(json.dumps(items,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
print('Recorded',len(items),'parser findings')
